{% assign block_settings = block.settings %}

{%- comment -%}
  One question. The markup mirrors blocks/_accordion-row.liquid so the FAQ page
  gets the theme's own disclosure behaviour -- a native <details>, keyboard
  operable, and expanded by find-in-page in current browsers -- instead of the
  legacy .accordion-title / .icon-close markup the previous theme used, whose
  CSS and click handler were never carried into this repo.

  Printing is NOT one of the things a closed <details> handles for you; the
  stylesheet below deals with it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% capture faq_item_children %}
  <details class="details ona-faq-item__details" data-testid="accordion-details" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <summary class="details__header">
      <h3 class="ona-faq-item__question">{{ block_settings.title | escape }}</h3>
      <span class="svg-wrapper icon-caret icon-animated">
        {{- 'icon-caret.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
      <span class="svg-wrapper icon-plus">
        {{- 'icon-plus.svg' | inline_asset_content -}}
      </span>
    </summary>

    <div class="details-content rte">
      {{ block_settings.content }}
    </div>
  </details>
{% endcapture %}
{% render 'accordion-custom-component', children: faq_item_children %}

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * The question is a heading so the FAQ page has a real document outline --
   * h1 page title > h2 category > h3 question. Neither the live theme's
   * <div class="accordion-title"> nor a bare <summary> gives one, and an
   * outline is what both search engines and screen reader rotors navigate by.
   *
   * `font: inherit` hands typography back to .accordion .details__header, so
   * this is purely semantic: the rendered result is identical to the plain
   * text it replaced. min-inline-size lets a long question wrap instead of
   * pushing the caret off the row -- a flex item defaults to min-width: auto.
   */
  .ona-faq-item__question {
    margin: 0;
    font: inherit;
    letter-spacing: inherit;
    text-transform: inherit;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }

  /*
   * A printed FAQ must carry its answers. Every row starts closed, and nothing
   * in the theme opens them for print -- there is no other @media print rule in
   * the repo -- so /pages/faq printed as fourteen questions with nothing under
   * them. Flagged by Codex on PR #192, against a comment above that had claimed
   * <details> handled print by itself. It does not; find-in-page it does.
   *
   * Three mechanisms hide the content and all three need answering: the theme's
   * own .details-content rule in snippets/accordion-custom-component.liquid,
   * the ::details-content pseudo-element browsers now use, and the older UA
   * rule that hides a closed details' non-summary children outright.
   */
  @media print {
    /*
     * These two must stay in SEPARATE rules. A selector list is invalid as a
     * whole if any one selector in it is, so pairing the class with
     * ::details-content means a browser that does not implement that
     * pseudo-element throws the rule away -- taking the legacy override with
     * it, in exactly the browsers that need it. Codex caught this in the first
     * version of this fix, where the two shared one selector list.
     */
    .ona-faq-item__details .details-content {
      block-size: auto;
      opacity: 1;
      overflow-y: visible;
    }

    .ona-faq-item__details::details-content {
      block-size: auto;
      opacity: 1;
      overflow-y: visible;
      content-visibility: visible;
    }

    .ona-faq-item__details:not([open]) > *:not(summary) {
      display: block;
    }

    /* The caret and plus mean nothing on paper. */
    .ona-faq-item__details .svg-wrapper {
      display: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "FAQ item",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Question"
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "content",
      "label": "Answer"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
